{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And may Elohim give you.</b> This is the attribute of justice, meaning, if you are worthy of it. But regarding Esav it is written: הנה משמני הארץ יהיה מושבך — whether worthy or not worthy. And likewise we find in the prayer of Solomon peace be upon him: regarding Israel he said, ועשית לאיש כדרכיו — for he would not be called a contentious disputant; and regarding the foreigner, ועשית ככל אשר יקרא אליך הנכרי וגו' — for otherwise he would be called a contentious disputant and would lodge complaints on high. And likewise you find ten blessings, corresponding to the ten utterances with which the world was created, and corresponding to the Ten Commandments. And in seven places he is blessed here and further on: ואל שדי יברך אותך; והנה ה' נצב עליו; ויאמר לא אשלחך כי אם ברכתני; וירא אלהים אל יעקב ויאמר אנכי אלהי אברהם אביך. And likewise Abraham was blessed with seven blessings: ואעשך לגוי גדול וגו'. Corresponding to them are seven festivals in the year: Shabbat, Pesach, Shavuot, Rosh HaShanah, Yom HaKippurim, Sukkot, Shemini Atzeret. And seven stars that shepherd and serve the sun and the moon. And seven that do not shepherd, and their name is Kesil. And the seven stars of Kimah: at the time it sets, the time has come to sow the earth, and when it rises, the time of harvest has arrived."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The single comment is long and contains multiple run-on scriptural citations presented without explicit addresses; these are rendered exactly as they appear. The term תגר is rendered 'contentious disputant' per its rabbinic usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:14.912359345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}